      "mergeID": "64540d2bdac5b0f260baf0e2",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Enabling avatar culling with someone's avatar hidden, before blocking someone, causes their hitbox to be pinned in place, making it easy to cheat most pvp-centric worlds.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "{BUG}Avatar Culling/Block bug",
      "parentID": "6452fcec3441c5092588cd82",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "640cd900cd696e451f368b53",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name}: I've tested this in Project Aincrad, Prison Escape, Site-19, and Let's Struggle. As far as I'm aware, Project Aincrad uses avatar contact-base hit registration, while the rest use a pill-style hitbox.",
